<li>I enjoyed the characterization quite a bit. I thought they were all spot-on, even Mr. Currie McCruelFace.</li>
<li>I liked the resolution.</li>
<li>I'm wondering if there's a tiny bit more than we're seeing here&#8230; clearly these goblins are extremely capable, and dangerous. Why/how were they wiped out? Currie seems to have an almost unnatural obsession with being cruel to them. Now, you address this, that he was just a &quot;bad apple,&quot; but what if its more than that? What if a certain percent of the population has a subconscious, ingrained, maybe even genetic hatred for them? Like babies as young as six months fear spiders and snakes&#8230; there's something in our genetic makeup that just tells us &quot;this thing is dangerous.&quot; Maybe it's the same thing with the goblins, and that's why they were systemically wiped out.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
